{
  "acceptance": [
    "A unit test following the pattern of tests/unit/core/throughput/test_stream_timing.py asserts refresh_stream.start_monotonic is taken after the refresh connection factory returns, and fails against the base commit when the factory sleeps.",
    "A test of compute_metrics with a sleeping refresh connection factory shows the Ts span excludes the connection setup time.",
    "test_throughput_duration_includes_refresh_precondition_and_postcondition_checks in tests/unit/core/throughput/test_tpch_refresh_timing.py is renamed or rewritten so its name states what it asserts; any other test in that file or in test_tpch_refresh.py whose name contradicts its assertions is likewise fixed (the PR lists the tests read).",
    "uv run -- pytest tests/unit/core/throughput tests/unit/core/tpch/test_tpch_refresh.py passes.",
    "If docs/internal/tpc-measured-intervals.md exists on the base branch, update the rows this change affects; otherwise append the row text to the context of tpc-measured-intervals-reference-20261103. docs/internal/throughput-result-alignment.md still matches the code, and the changelog states the effect on Ts."
  ],
  "batch": {
    "batch_id": "tpch-refresh-path",
